WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.501
-Our next guest is
a very funny comedian,

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.403
you know, from his work
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:07.340
The 49th season of "SNL"
kicks off this Saturday,

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.342
October 14th on NBC
and streams live on Peacock

00:00:10.342 --> 00:00:13.646
with host Pete Davidson
and musical guest Ice Spice.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:16.916
Please welcome to the show.
Marcello Hernandez, everybody.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.118
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:40.540 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.375
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:45.144
Marcello, this is, uh,

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:46.412
I want to get this
out of the way.

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:48.915
This is your first appearance
on a talk show.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.016
-Yes.
Can you tell?

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:52.018
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.586
-It's just -- it's amazing that
you know

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:58.324
all the customs --
tuxedo, corsage for the host,

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.927
bottle of wine
with no glasses or corkscrew.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:03.429
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:06.365
This is so -- I'm so happy.
I really love this.

00:01:06.365 --> 00:01:07.867
I'm going to take it off
only because I'm worried

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:11.403
I'm going to poke your eye out,
but -- I talk with my hands.

00:01:11.403 --> 00:01:13.640
Congratulations on
an exceptional first season

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.708
on the show.
-Oh, thank you so much.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.476
Thank you. Thank you, guys.

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:19.044
-I hope this is true,

00:01:19.044 --> 00:01:21.915
but when I watch
new cast members

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.282
and I think
the first time

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:25.184
I really took stock of you
was behind the Update Desk.

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.086
You seemed like you were
having a very good time,

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.789
which is a very hard thing to do
on a stressful show like that.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.924
But I think one of the reasons
the audience likes to see you

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:33.626
is you seem
to be enjoying yourself.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.228
-I absolutely am.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.696
I used to sell tickets
on the street in New York,

00:01:37.696 --> 00:01:41.334
so there's nothing
to not be happy about.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.835
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:46.472
There's no reason for me not to
be having the time of my life.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.441
-Well, it definitely shows.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:49.776
And it's very exciting
to have you back.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.978
And also, I was backstage.
Your mom is here tonight.

00:01:52.978 --> 00:01:54.480
-My mom is here today.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.514
-I think she is right
over there.

00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:57.383
-There she is.
Yes, that's my mom!

00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.219
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:01.554
I -- can I say something
to here?

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:03.356
-You can say whatever
you like to your mom.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.024
-Mom, very quickly,
I just want to say

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.359
I am so grateful for you

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.826
and everything that
you sacrificed for me

00:02:07.826 --> 00:02:09.695
in my life
and everything I do,

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:11.497
including this,
is always for you.

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:14.701
[ Speaking in Spanish ]

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:15.868
-Aww.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.738
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.606
That is so sweet.

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:23.343
And also it's funny because
I was in the dressing room

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:25.011
and you walked out
and I said to your mom,

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.846
You must be so proud of him.
And she went, "Eh."

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.382
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.550
-That's -- that sounds like her.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.085
Yes, that sounds like her.

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:34.354
-I'm joking, of course.

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:37.390
But you -- you did a sketch
with Pedro Pascal...

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.291
-Yes.
...who was. a really wonderful

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:40.292
season of host last year,

00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:41.728
but he did stand out.
-Yes.

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:44.263
-And he played
an overprotective mother.

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:47.900
And there's a Pedro
with a mustache,

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.035
which is very funny to me.

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:52.505
And was this based
at all on your mom?

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.741
-Not physically.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:56.508
-I think that is clear.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.508 --> 00:02:58.544
It's almost why it was good
to have a cut to

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.847
of your beautiful mother, yeah.
-Thank you.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.049
He came to the show
and he kind of had this idea

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.817
of wanting to do something
in Spanish,

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.185
and he wanted to be my mother.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:09.054
It was, you know, he kind of had
this vibe coming in,

00:03:09.054 --> 00:03:11.291
and I was lucky enough to be
the only person at the show

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.825
that could write in Spanish.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:15.461
And it just gave me
the great opportunity.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:18.164
So, Pedro, my second mom,
thank you. I love you.

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:19.766
-And what are some of
the things that I know

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:21.100
it's based on actual thing.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.268
What were some things
your mom would say?

00:03:23.268 --> 00:03:25.204
-Well...
-You knew as as somebody

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.638
with a sense of humor
were funny things?

00:03:26.638 --> 00:03:29.242
-Well, the great line --
one of the pieces of the sketch

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:32.711
is that my mother
doesn't believe in ADD.

00:03:32.711 --> 00:03:37.649
And so one of the lines
is my son don't have ADD.

00:03:37.649 --> 00:03:38.918
He just liked to jump.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:41.054
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:46.692
So that kind of sounds
like her.

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:49.295
-You you took advantage
of being able to write

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.763
in Spanish multiple times
last year.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.631
-Yes.
-Ana de Armas was on.

00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:54.133
-Oh, wow.
And you wrote --

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:57.003
this is -- it was
a Spanish class.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:04:00.106
And you grew up in Miami,
but you went to college in Ohio

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:02.641
and you did a take
Spanish in college.

00:04:02.641 --> 00:04:04.610
-Yes, I took --

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.946
I wanted
to feel smart in school.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.914
-Yeah.
-So I took the hardest class

00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:11.250
that they had, you know,
Spanish one million.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.685
And it was so funny to me

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.754
because the teachers
in the Spanish classes

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.456
in the Midwest,
they have American names.

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:18.523
You know, I walked in
and my teacher's name was,

00:04:18.523 --> 00:04:19.725
you know, Seth Meyers,

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:21.894
like something like --
just like a name

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.662
that you knew immediately
you were going to be like,

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:25.331
oh, I'm better
than this person.

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.599
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.599 --> 00:04:28.801
And it was just shocking.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.336
Like, I remember
one of the times,

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.638
like the first day everybody
introduces themselves

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:35.975
and, you know, the ladies like,
"Jake, por favor?"

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:39.778
And he's like, "Hola,
mi nombre es Jake

00:04:39.778 --> 00:04:43.216
and yo soy from Cincinnati

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:46.886
and mi comida
favorito es pizza.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.521
And then I'm like,
"No, now me, please, me.

00:04:49.521 --> 00:04:54.961
And I'm like...
[ Speaking in Spanish ]

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:58.530
And then the teachers just like,
"Did you guys hear that?

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.133
That is your new teacher."

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.735
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.070
[ Applause ]

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:08.975
Now, you actually --
a college athlete.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.242 line:0%
-Yes.
-Played soccer in college?

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:11.744 line:0%
-Yes, John Carroll University.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.312 line:0%
-There you go.
I love to see this.

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:15.715 line:0%
And then because you did
a wonderful thing

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:19.251
at the Update Desk
about a Latin baseball players

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:21.254
and how they celebrate
differently,

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:22.688
they interview differently.

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:24.356
They have more style,
more flair.

00:05:24.356 --> 00:05:26.191
And you actually
got to participate

00:05:26.191 --> 00:05:28.060
in the All-Star game this year.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.295
-Yes.
-There you are looking like

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:31.130
you know what you're doing.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.866
But even more impressive,
I want to show a clip

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:36.402
because I've done -- I threw out
a first pitch once.

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:37.904
I was so nervous.

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:40.306
And you walking up to bat
in this celebrity

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:43.609
all-star game
seemed very chill and loose.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.545
And I'll show it first
and then ask you a question.

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:47.846
Let's watch Marcello
walking to the plate.

00:05:47.846 --> 00:05:49.649
-Oh.

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:52.618
Is a New Yorker?

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:54.654
-Wait a minute.
-It seems like he could be.

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:57.123
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:59.892
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:06.666
-Yeah, I-I definitely did that.

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:09.635
-I think my favorite, I really
enjoyed that update feature,

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:13.072
the many observations you have
about Latin baseball players.

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:15.007
One is just the pulling out
of the chain.

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.642
-Of course.
-Which is --

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.544
Can you explain real quick?

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.413
-I think it's just, one,
it's to be maybe

00:06:20.413 --> 00:06:21.814
a little more comfortable
out there.

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:26.451
But they have a few chains,
and some of it is religious.

00:06:26.451 --> 00:06:28.354
You know what I mean?
They're always -- they always

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:31.023
have like a, you know,
a crucifix or something.

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:33.692
And, yeah, I think
they're just cool that way.

00:06:33.692 --> 00:06:35.361
They pull out their chain.

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:36.595
They're like,
in the name of the father

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:38.364
and the Son and the Holy Spirit,
they thank people.

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:40.600
It's like such
a beautiful experience.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.833
I used to have a joke
I did on stage

00:06:41.833 --> 00:06:43.936
where the batter would be like,

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:45.437
you know,
in the name of the Father, Son,

00:06:45.437 --> 00:06:47.607
Holy Ghost, just in case I need
a little divine intervention.

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:48.608
[ Chuckles ]

00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:51.644
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:54.147
And they're so ready afterwards.

00:06:54.147 --> 00:06:56.616
-Did you -- when you auditioned
for SNL,

00:06:56.616 --> 00:06:58.918
were you pulling from
from old standup?

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.020
Did you at least know?
Oh, I'm doing stuff

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.588
that's worked on stage
and have a little bit

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.022
more confidence because of that.

00:07:04.022 --> 00:07:05.558
-1,000%.

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:09.195
A lot of my audition material
was about my mom

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:12.464
and about how
she escaped communism.

00:07:12.464 --> 00:07:15.334
And I'd be like, Mom,
"I had a bad day at school."

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.069
And she'd be like,
"Oh, yeah?

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:19.172
[ Laughter ]

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.675
At the place
with the free food?

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:24.710
That's...?"

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.146
So a lot of the stuff
was kind of about that stuff.

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:29.848
And she -- she's my inspiration,
my muse.

00:07:29.848 --> 00:07:33.685
-Yeah, well, I'll tell you,
the more you talk about her,

00:07:33.685 --> 00:07:35.220
the more it makes sense
that you look like you're having

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.423
so much fun on stage.
You seem very grateful.

00:07:37.423 --> 00:07:40.826
And I am very grateful
for both you and your mom

00:07:40.826 --> 00:07:42.094
for making you the guy you are

00:07:42.094 --> 00:07:43.529
because you're so much fun
to watch.

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:45.064
Congratulations. Can't wait
to see your second season.

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:46.064
-Thank you so much.

00:07:46.064 --> 00:07:47.366
-Thanks for being here,
Marcello.

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:48.968
You guys, Marcello Hernandez.

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:50.836
"SNL" returns live

00:07:50.836 --> 00:07:52.170
for its season premiere
this week

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:54.473
with host Pete Davidson
and musical guest Ice Spice.

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:56.108
We'll be right back
with the very funny

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:57.210
Aparna Nancherla.

